WEBVTT

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:50.910
"The Ones Within"

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:17.700
--Ah, Akki's antenna hair is simply the best.
--Did you try the mushroom?

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.830
Huh? That was a mushroom?

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.660
I keep it healthy by--

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:26.830
Everyone's here...
Thank you for gathering today.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:32.450
I-I would like to begin Game 9
if it's not too much trouble...

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:36.450
Uh, but if you can't, tomorrow is fine, too...

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:37.910
We can't hear you.

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:42.250
Mr. Paka, what's wrong?
Why don't you come any closer?

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:46.080
Well, since I'm universally
hated after last time,

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:49.410
I wasn't sure of the best way
to approach you all today.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:51.370
Like I care.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:55.830
Mr. Kudou and Ms. Sarayashiki
are looking at me like I'm trash.

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:58.040
Don't worry, I always have.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:01.750
And Mr. Onigasaki has his hand on his katana.

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:03.160
I always do.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:04.790
Is that right?

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:08.790
Mr. Paka, I've gotten over it already.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:11.700
M-Mr. Iride!

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:15.410
Ahem! Then, let's try this again...

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:20.200
"Congrats"
"50,000,000 views!"
"Halfway There!"

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:26.330
Congratulations are in order!
Congrats on reaching 50,000,000 views!

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:30.250
At this rate, getting 100,000,000
views may not be a dream!

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:34.200
So without further ado,
let's go all out again today!

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.160
Game 9 time!

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:40.450
Yeah!

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:41.870
"Laboratory #3"

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:45.120
"Laboratory #3"
To celebrate reaching 50,000,000 views,

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:50.160
I've prepared a virtual simulation
for all of you to enjoy!

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.000
First, we'll synchronize your avatars.
To your capsules, please.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.080
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes!

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:59.250
It's just like cryogenic sleep!

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.120
Huh? What's that?

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:06.120
Artificial hibernation. Happens
all the time in science fiction.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.540
Close me in!

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:09.370
--It's technology to preserve life
at low temperatures.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:11.200
--Close me in!
--It's technology to preserve life
at low temperatures.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:17.040
--Close it! Close me in, please!
--Because an incurable illness now
might become curable in the future.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.750
Incurable illness...

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:24.290
--Anya...
--We'll now commence synchronizing
your personality data.

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:29.000
Close your capsule lid and please
lie down and wait a moment.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.200
Ouch!

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:49.750
Ow, ow, ow! Please, stop! You'll pull it out!

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.120
Meow!

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:02.450
Game 9 is "The Ones Within Kindergarten."

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:04.410
Those playing the parent role...

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:09.200
...are to do your best to get along
with these kindergartners.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.370
So cute!

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:13.370
These kids are "Instant Avatars."

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:18.500
The plants atop their heads will grow
according to their affection level.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:21.290
Clear the game by making
three or more blossom.

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:23.750
There's all sorts of blossoms, too.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:26.450
Wait... Can we all just wait?

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:27.540
Yes?

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:30.080
Are these children the real thing?

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:32.160
No, no, of course not.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:35.040
They're an improved breed
of Mimicry Man-eaters.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:39.080
Using an AI chip, they act
like the person themselves.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.910
But since the original person is synchronized,

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:45.540
they can't exit the capsule
until the game is finished.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:48.250
So you mean, if we're unable to clear it...

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:53.660
Naturally, they'll continue
sleeping for eternity.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.790
Incidentally, this same group...

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:58.540
"Stage 2" "Ouija Exchange"
"Grant the spirit's three wishes
and obtain 'Chromosome 01.'"
...has previously participated in a stage together.

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:02.450
...has previously participated in a stage together.

00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:05.540
I'm looking forward to seeing what you've got.

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:11.200
With the games resuming, we'll see
how strong your bonds truly are.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:13.750
Now then, you must excuse me.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.910
Screw you, asshole!

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:26.500
Now, now. Why don't you
come over here, Himiko?

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:32.620
It's all right. He really needs
to put away his scary face, right?

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:34.410
Who are you talkin' about?!

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:40.830
Oh? Would Yuzu like a hug, too?

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:43.290
Meow!

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:46.160
My back will totally feel this tomorrow...

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:49.910
So be it then...

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:52.080
Come on, Onigasaki.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:02.290
What are you sighing for?

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:08.040
Aikawa, you come, too.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:14.370
Don't sleep. He's smaller but still the same.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:16.620
What are we supposed to do now?

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:19.620
Seeing how it's around noon,
how about lunchtime?

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:21.370
Sushi! Sushi!

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:22.620
And nap after lunch.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:26.200
You guys are suddenly seasoned
mothers out of nowhere.

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:30.040
Anya, you should face the other way.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:31.250
What the hell for?!

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.580
It's hard to say, but you know...

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:35.160
--Huh? What are you getting at?!

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.120
--I know! Let's make silly faces then!
--Huh? What are you getting at?!

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:38.950
Huh?! You really are...

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:51.250
All right, everyone! Hands together!

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:56.000
Father, Mother, Mr. Paka...
Thank you for the yummy food!

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:58.080
Thank you.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.080
Okay! Let's eat!

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.910
Let's eat!

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:02.830
"---ka Pudding"
Let's eat!

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:06.620
"---ka Pudding"
Why do all of us have kids' meals, too?

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:10.870
By eating and drinking what they do,
we can understand the kids better.

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:13.950
Don't lie. You just wanted to eat it, right?

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:17.790
The toy that comes with it
tickles my urge to collect.

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:18.660
I've almost completed the Mr. Paka series!

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:20.830
"Learning Book"
"Paka Paka Learning Book"
I've almost completed the Mr. Paka series!

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:22.830
"Learning Book"
"Paka Paka Learning Book"
Stop or he'll get full of himself.

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:26.910
I got a second Paka-ear headband,
so I'll give the extra to Anya.

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:30.620
Put that on me and I'm
never talking to you again.

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:32.700
Huh? But why?

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:34.000
Sheesh...

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:41.250
What the hell?

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.750
Again? Punitsuki, house!

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:48.290
--Puni puni!
--Ow, ow, ow, ow! This isn't your damn house!

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:54.040
Stop yelling. You're just scaring them.

00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:58.700
Wh-What?

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:01.370
Oshigiri is touching a girl all on his own!

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:04.410
--Wha...?
--It's worse that he's fine with lolis!

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.750
Quit saying weird things!

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:08.870
How about with Yuzu then?

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:10.620
U-Uh...

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:13.120
He draws an odd line.

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:14.660
Me, too!

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:21.290
"Paka Pudd--"

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:29.580
Don't give up like that.

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:33.910
Anyway, how do we make 'em blossom?

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:36.620
We have to raise their affection, right?

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:40.700
This sort of stuff is Himiko
and Makino's forte, but...

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:43.040
They're both devouring a kids' meal.

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:47.290
Himiko, you sure love rolled omelettes, huh?

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:51.080
You can have mine, too.

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:00.950
Ooh, it's a bud!

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:03.250
Woohoo! Let's keep it up!

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:04.620
You fed her...

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:11.830
I think smiling is the first step
of building affection.

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:13.160
Smiling?

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:15.870
And you guys don't smile all that much.

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:19.950
Oshigiri wears a mask... Karin gets so cranky...

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:23.830
And Anya only laughs to
scorn and insult other people.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:29.160
Little kids like these watch our
expressions a lot more than you think.

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:32.250
Akki, um... I ate bubbles.

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:34.660
Smiling... It's important.

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:39.830
--Hey, hey, Akki! Bubbles, bubbles, bubbles!
--Oh! Right, right. You're from planet Bubbles.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:44.620
--Sushi!
--Onigasaki!

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:45.950
Oy?

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:49.290
I-It's time to brush your teeth.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:53.120
Oy, oy!

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:56.250
Onigasaki.

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:57.410
Oy?!

00:10:57.410 --> 00:10:59.700
Come sit on my lap.

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:02.160
Sushi!

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:04.910
I love that part of Kaikoku.

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:12.660
Aikawa. Need to pee before napping?

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:25.660
Aikawa is acting strange?

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:29.660
I wouldn't say strange.
Just more mellow than usual.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:31.330
He won't even look at me.

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.660
Isn't that how he always is?

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:36.000
Oh, now that you mention it...

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:39.910
Only Aikawa's sprout is as small as it started.

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:43.370
He's never been one to be
assertive and talk, but...

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:45.830
I'm just... sort of worried.

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:43.540
"Shirasu"
"I love you."

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:46.790
"Makino Aikawa"
"Sumire (Maiden name Mukai)"
"Kindly circle if you will be celebrating with us."

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:58.080
Makino...

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:01.870
Makino!

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:04.870
Thank goodness!

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:08.700
You were having a nightmare.
Are you all right?

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:21.080
I love you!

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:22.620
Hey!

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:24.910
Hey! Come here, quick!

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:28.500
Ooh!

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:32.500
I pet her, hugged her, and when I gave
her a rolled omelette, it blossomed!

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:34.870
Rolled omelettes sure are amazing.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:35.750
Right?

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:38.750
Th-That's not why! It was my love!

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:40.620
Gotta respect them eggs.

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:42.330
--Right?!
--Hey now!

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:44.000
Tone it down.

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:48.160
You're a lot friendlier
than I thought you'd be.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:49.120
Sushi!

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:50.830
You just ate some.

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:56.160
To think you were so earnest and cute...

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:58.700
I wonder where it all went wrong.

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:01.450
"Open-Air Outdoor Bath"

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:03.910
I take my socks off!

00:14:03.910 --> 00:14:06.160
Yeah? That's impressive!

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:11.500
It's the dude's bath for you.

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:13.000
Calm your ass down!

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:15.450
It's fine with me.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:20.040
He's little anyway. And it's not like
he's the real Onigasaki, right?

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:21.830
It's fine.

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:23.370
Come with me!

00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:32.450
Hi! I'm Akki!

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:33.790
They blossomed.

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:35.290
That ain't no blossom!

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:40.120
What's your deal? He said there could
be all sorts of blossoms, right?

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:42.580
That's stinky and that's plain creepy!

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:45.870
Don't let me be the only sane one!
The burden's too much!

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:49.750
All three of them blossomed
when they were with you. No fair...

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:53.330
No big deal, right? We all
got to see them in the end.

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:57.910
♪ Ding dong, ding neigh. ♪

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:02.790
Stage 9 cleared. Congratulations
on getting three blossoms.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:06.750
Your bonds were so strong,
it must have been an easy win.

00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:08.700
'Course it was, moron.

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:12.950
The clear condition has been met,
so this game is officially over.

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:17.620
Please send a representative
to accept Chromosome 08.

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:20.080
I'll see you tomorrow.

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:30.290
My, this is odd...

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:35.290
You achieved three blossoms which
means you've cleared the game, yet...

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:37.370
You saying that on purpose?

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:39.290
Neigh...

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:41.200
Well, all right...

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:46.370
It'll be troublesome if you boycott again,
so please finish by morning.

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:50.040
The next game is waiting for you.

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:51.620
Blossom!

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:55.040
You wanna be little like this
for the rest of your life?!

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:57.080
Quit it. Don't intimidate him.

00:15:57.080 --> 00:16:00.290
Shuddap! It's your fault
for going easy on him!

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:02.830
Who would open their heart via force?

00:16:02.830 --> 00:16:05.700
What Aikawa's heart needs is a blanket.

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:07.410
Poetic and creepy!

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:12.750
Hey, hey. Save the fighting for later, meow.

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:15.080
Guys, you're back to normal!

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:16.540
Thanks to you.

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:20.000
Wait... Then those kids are...

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:26.290
Their synchronization cut off.

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:31.330
Littlegasaki...

00:16:35.540 --> 00:16:37.540
What are you sighing about?

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:42.540
Here! This one's mine, right?
It's mine, right? Woohoo!

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:51.750
All right! It's time to begin
Operation Makimaki Blossom!

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:53.500
Yay!

00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:58.330
First up is Himi and Karirin's
giant Murasaki cake!

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:05.120
Next up is Akki and the Pandarou tower tour!

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:07.200
We're dead if we fall!

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:09.950
Anboy's bubble blowing course!

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:11.910
Sixty-second shoulder ride!

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:15.620
Playing house! Hide and seek!
Full-body massage!

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:18.660
Soft-boiled egg gymnastics! Afro!

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:24.160
I-Is it growing?

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:25.660
Slightly?

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:27.160
It's iffy.

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:32.580
Did you decide what you'll do, Zak?

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:34.700
I'm not sure...

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:37.080
Aren't you two the same age?

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:40.040
How about calling him his name like a friend?

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:41.410
Wh-What?

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:43.330
Oh, I like that idea!

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:46.410
D-Do you think that would
really help him blossom?

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:49.580
Not like I'm against it or anything...

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:50.370
You're sick.

00:17:50.370 --> 00:17:52.000
Excuse me?!

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.040
You're sick!

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:54.660
--What do you mean by sick?!
--What about you?

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:57.040
--Sick as in I wanna throw up!
--I've been doing it this whole time.

00:17:57.040 --> 00:17:58.660
--Well, I'm sick of you!
--I'm giving him big hugs.

00:17:58.660 --> 00:17:59.830
--You wanna piece, you jerk?!
--I'm giving him big hugs.

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:03.290
--You wanna piece, you jerk?!
--Doesn't this feel so warm, Makimaki?

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:14.910
"Laboratory #3"

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:20.200
Isn't the moon pretty tonight?

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:25.540
Shall we talk about love for a bit?

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:28.830
You see, I don't remember the past.

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:32.000
My mom right now isn't my biological one,

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:36.540
but she's cheerful and smiles
a lot... and I love her.

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:41.370
Sometimes she doesn't really
see me, but that's fine.

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:43.540
Because I love her.

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:47.040
It's fine.

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:52.580
Is there somebody you
love right now, Makino?

00:18:52.580 --> 00:18:58.500
If you love somebody, I think it's fine
if they don't return the feeling.

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:00.540
They might not look at you,

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:06.000
and you might not be who matters
most to them, but it happens.

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:09.370
Can you not be happy with that, Makino?

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:13.540
If you can accept it,

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:15.660
it won't hurt anymore.

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:21.910
So accept it... and keep moving forward.

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:28.160
Accept it?

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:38.580
The people who gave birth to me...
won't look at me.

00:19:38.580 --> 00:19:42.370
The person Sumire loves... isn't me.

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:24.200
Accept it.

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:39.500
Accept it.

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:47.750
My heart... was broken.

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:53.370
Why did that happen?

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:55.660
I don't know... I don't know, but...

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:58.160
We're short on time! Say it, Zak!

00:20:58.160 --> 00:20:59.910
Uh...

00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:05.580
Ma... Ma...

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:10.160
Ma... Ma... Ma... Ma... Ma...

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:12.200
S-Sorry.

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:18.120
I've always had trouble
calling people by their names.

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:22.700
But I really do want to get
closer to you, Aikawa.

00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:25.200
That's why, uh...

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:30.910
Do you think, from now on,
I could call you Makino?

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:39.660
Aikaw-- I mean, Makino.

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:41.080
So cringeworthy.

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:42.500
Onigasaki!

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:44.370
Look, it's blossoming!

00:22:09.080 --> 00:22:14.750
Now then, it's about time
for the real fun to begin.
